  "slug": "sequences-promoter-38cf",
  "summary": "New glycan-specific pose metrics, a bias-aware scoring benchmark, and structure-free affinity predictors shift evaluation away from coordinate agreement alone.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the evaluation layer around binding prediction rather than the generators themselves. CARVE defines glycan-specific pose-quality criteria (oRMSD, irRMSD, Fnat with DP-scaled thresholds) across 1,974 protein-glycan complexes, acknowledging that generic interface RMSD conventions do not transfer to carbohydrate chemistry. HiFiPL-Bench curates a fidelity-first, bias-aware set from PDB and BindingDB to diagnose nine protein-ligand scoring functions, and ShEPhERD-score supplies GPU-accelerated differentiable 3D similarity and alignment benchmarked on DUDE-Z virtual screening. In parallel, affinity estimation is being detached from docked coordinates: STORM and Savant predict affinity or dissociation constants from sequence and SMILES with leakage-controlled splits, while BioLM-Score conditions residue-atom geometric likelihoods on frozen language-model embeddings. Interface prediction follows, with HandShake doing sequence-only partner-specific interface calls via ProstT5 and cross-chain attention, and TopoPPI mapping interfaces into low-distortion 2D atlases.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-20"
}
